Feature: F3 null-union — KNOWN-STOP (promote to a positive scenario the day it closes)

  Scenario: an interface cannot yet be a null-union member
    Given source inline = """
    type Shape = interface { fn area(self) -> i64 }
    type Square = class & Shape {
        pub side: i64
        pub fn make(s: i64) -> Square { Square { side = s } }
        pub fn area(self) -> i64 { self.side * self.side }
    }
    let present: Shape | null = Square::make(6)
    exit(1)
    """
    When compilation fails
    Then diagnostic = "interface cannot be a variant member"
